1
00:00:09,230 --> 00:00:10,350
(Passenger Drop-off Area)

2
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:39,380
=Vow of Autumn=
=Episode 6=

3
00:01:05,219 --> 00:01:07,579
You seem pretty comfortable
driving my car.

4
00:01:08,079 --> 00:01:08,980
Don't do that again.

5
00:01:10,599 --> 00:01:11,140
What?

6
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:13,120
Fight.

7
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:16,359
He tried to hit you first.

8
00:01:16,519 --> 00:01:17,840
If a dog bites, you bite back?

9
00:01:17,959 --> 00:01:18,760
Are you a dog?

10
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:24,099
Then why did you raise your hand?

11
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,519
You were going to hit him too.

12
00:01:27,079 --> 00:01:28,560
By your own logic,

13
00:01:29,379 --> 00:01:30,299
what kind of dog are you?

14
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:38,060
I'd say

15
00:01:38,680 --> 00:01:40,319
you're the kind that looks fierce

16
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:43,040
but can't put up much of a fight.

17
00:01:44,079 --> 00:01:44,780
Like...

18
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:46,120
a Samoyed.

19
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,280
You're the Samoyed!

20
00:01:53,859 --> 00:01:54,900
I'm a guard dog.

21
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:56,099
If anyone hurts you,

22
00:01:56,459 --> 00:01:57,280
I'll bite them.

23
00:02:02,439 --> 00:02:03,799
Calling yourself a dog now?

24
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:06,099
Woof!

25
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:12,039
Enough.

26
00:02:12,099 --> 00:02:12,840
Stop kidding.

27
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:13,719
Let's go back.

28
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:14,979
Let me treat your wound.

29
00:02:58,460 --> 00:02:58,840
Your hand.

30
00:03:21,813 --> 00:03:22,866
(Medicine chest)

31
00:03:23,453 --> 00:03:24,580
(Band-Aid)

32
00:03:34,419 --> 00:03:34,939
Done.

33
00:04:38,779 --> 00:04:39,600
Do you...

34
00:04:40,399 --> 00:04:41,480
want to use the bathroom?

35
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:48,860
I'm fine.

36
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:50,639
I'll just sit here a bit.

37
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:56,439
Water?

38
00:04:56,579 --> 00:04:56,860
Yes.

39
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:13,199
I didn't know you could hit that hard.

40
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:21,759
I used to practice boxing.

41
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:24,839
Why did you take it up?

42
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,800
You don't have to tell me.

43
00:05:39,279 --> 00:05:41,319
A girl once told me

44
00:05:42,519 --> 00:05:44,279
she liked guys who could fight.

45
00:05:51,879 --> 00:05:53,680
So you learned just for her?

46
00:05:56,439 --> 00:05:57,319
Pretty much.

47
00:06:00,639 --> 00:06:01,319
Your first love?

48
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:08,959
How devoted.

49
00:06:12,360 --> 00:06:13,519
She means a lot to me.

50
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:25,160
Feeling better? Off you go.

51
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:36,319
I'd like to stay a bit longer.

52
00:06:37,439 --> 00:06:38,079
Go already.

53
00:06:53,959 --> 00:06:54,399
Oh,

54
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:55,480
wait a second.

55
00:06:55,493 --> 00:06:56,379
(Cheng A J5630)

56
00:07:03,560 --> 00:07:04,379
Almost forgot this.

57
00:07:05,199 --> 00:07:06,160
It was all going well,

58
00:07:06,259 --> 00:07:07,699
but that jerk caused a scene,

59
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:09,439
so your tarts went cold again.

60
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:13,600
Thanks. Get home safe.

61
00:07:19,399 --> 00:07:20,040
Oh,

62
00:07:20,860 --> 00:07:23,959
if you do win back your first love,

63
00:07:24,199 --> 00:07:25,639
bring her to meet me.

64
00:07:25,959 --> 00:07:27,160
After all,

65
00:07:27,319 --> 00:07:28,560
I'm like your big sister.

66
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:29,600
I'll size her up.

67
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:31,279
Bye.

68
00:07:59,980 --> 00:08:01,639
(That girl I told you about...)

69
00:08:02,060 --> 00:08:02,699
(It's you.)

70
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:05,160
(Pei Yiqiu)
I've had feelings for you for years.

71
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:07,040
(Ever since I first saw you.)

72
00:08:09,680 --> 00:08:12,920
(I'll change the kitchen bulb
for you tomorrow.)

73
00:08:49,519 --> 00:08:50,600
What do you think

74
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,360
of our class monitor's looks?

75
00:08:51,360 --> 00:08:52,600
I think he's pretty handsome.

76
00:08:54,759 --> 00:08:56,120
Too small. Looks weak.

77
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:58,000
Small?

78
00:08:58,159 --> 00:08:59,200
He's 1.8 meters tall!

79
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:00,320
So what?

80
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:01,639
A breeze could topple him.

81
00:09:01,879 --> 00:09:03,480
In the 1,000-meter run in PE class,

82
00:09:03,840 --> 00:09:04,639
he was second-last.

83
00:09:04,799 --> 00:09:05,679
Even I was faster.

84
00:09:07,759 --> 00:09:09,399
Then what's your type?

85
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:12,840
I like guys

86
00:09:13,539 --> 00:09:14,820
who can fight.

87
00:09:16,159 --> 00:09:18,039
Like Zhou Yan in the next class.

88
00:09:18,559 --> 00:09:19,639
Last time, outside school,

89
00:09:19,799 --> 00:09:21,320
he took down three punks on his own.

90
00:09:22,039 --> 00:09:23,600
Now that's hot.

91
00:09:24,419 --> 00:09:24,779
Wait.

92
00:09:24,919 --> 00:09:26,200
All he has is muscles.

93
00:09:26,399 --> 00:09:27,440
He'd make me feel safe.

94
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:28,620
If anything happened,

95
00:09:28,620 --> 00:09:30,080
he'd stand in front to protect me.

96
00:09:37,706 --> 00:09:39,573
(Martial arts)

97
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:40,759
(Well?)

98
00:09:41,279 --> 00:09:41,679
(Stop!)

99
00:09:42,639 --> 00:09:44,240
(Relax your shoulders.)

100
00:09:44,559 --> 00:09:45,639
(Rotate your hips.)

101
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:46,519
(Come and watch.)

102
00:09:47,034 --> 00:09:48,281
(Martial arts)

103
00:09:49,139 --> 00:09:50,100
(Got it? You try.)

104
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:51,480
(Remember what I said.)

105
00:09:53,039 --> 00:09:53,480
(Yes.)

106
00:09:54,279 --> 00:09:55,120
(Better.)

107
00:10:02,519 --> 00:10:03,159
(One, two.)

108
00:10:05,279 --> 00:10:05,960
(One, two.)

109
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:23,900
(Cheng A J5630)

110
00:10:45,873 --> 00:10:47,421
(Passenger Drop-off Area)
